From: Husky <hyiy666@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] qca-nss-clients: fix pppoe lifecycle, vlan unlock bug, qdisc unwind, and of_node leaks

1. In pppoe/nss_connmgr_pppoe.c:
   - Remove premature dev_put() in nss_connmgr_pppoe_get_session() so opt.dev
     remains held by dev_hold() during connect; pair dev_put(opt.dev) at the
     end of connect and error unwinds.
   - Embed struct rcu_head in struct nss_connmgr_pppoe_session_entry and switch
     to non-blocking kfree_rcu(), eliminating synchronize_rcu() stalls.
   - Always call nss_unregister_pppoe_session_if() and dealloc dynamic interface
     on disconnect even when firmware message fails, preventing dangling entries.
2. In vlan/nss_vlan_mgr.c:
   - Remove unbalanced spin_unlock(&vlan_mgr_ctx.lock) in nss_vlan_mgr_delete_bond_slave().
   - Modernize sysctl registration to register_sysctl("nss/vlan_client", ...) for Linux 6.18.
3. In nss_qdisc/nss_qdisc.c:
   - Consolidate qdisc registration into a loop with full reverse unwinding on failure.
4. Across pppoe, netlink, wifi_meshmgr, qdisc:
   - Add of_node_put() calls after of_find_node_by_name(NULL, "nss-common").

Signed-off-by: Husky <hyiy666@gmail.com>
---
--- a/netlink/nss_nl.c
+++ b/netlink/nss_nl.c
@@ -478,9 +478,11 @@ static int __init nss_nl_init(void)
 	/*
 	 * If the node is not compatible, don't do anything.
 	 */
-	if (!of_find_node_by_name(NULL, "nss-common")) {
+	struct device_node *cmn = of_find_node_by_name(NULL, "nss-common");
+	if (!cmn) {
 		return 0;
 	}
+	of_node_put(cmn);
 #endif
 	nss_nl_info_always("NSS Netlink manager loaded: %s\n", NSS_CLIENT_BUILD_ID);

@@ -521,9 +523,11 @@ static void __exit nss_nl_exit(void)
 	/*
 	 * If the node is not compatible, don't do anything.
 	 */
-	if (!of_find_node_by_name(NULL, "nss-common")) {
+	struct device_node *cmn = of_find_node_by_name(NULL, "nss-common");
+	if (!cmn) {
 		return;
 	}
+	of_node_put(cmn);
 #endif
 	nss_nl_info_always("NSS Netlink manager unloaded\n");

